// Simple White Noise: TV static.
// Each pixel gets a uniform gray value from a hash of its integer position and a seed that changes every frame.
// The hash uses only floating point math, so that the translation to OpenGL works. Bit operations, uint and
// derivative functions are avoided for the same reason.
//
// hash13 is from "Hash without Sine" by David Hoskins (https://www.shadertoy.com/view/4djSRW), ported to HLSL:
//
// MIT License...
/* Copyright (c)2014 David Hoskins.

Permission is hereby granted, free of charge, to any person obtaining a copy
